digraph ReasoningTree {
  // paper_id=s41467-025-56857-z
  rankdir="TB";
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper investigates whether the lupus-associated Ncf1 R90H mutation, which lowers ROS production, produces severe systemic lupus erythematosus in mice only in combination with murine norovirus infection, thereby testing a specific gene-environment virus synergy and comparing it with pristane exposure alone.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When lupus risk is genetically complex and environmental triggers remain uncertain, defined mouse models can be used to test whether a candidate genetic susceptibility factor interacts with specific exposures such as virus infection or pristane."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) NCF1-regulated interferon and lupus-associated phenotypes can become apparent after environmental challenges such as immunization or pristane, supporting the use of challenge conditions when studying Ncf1-mutant lupus models."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) The animal-model evidence includes Ncf1 T153M-associated autoimmune disease in rats and spontaneous Ncf1 m1J mutation phenotypes in mice, including lupus-related manifestations."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) Given the polygenic SLE background and the conditional relevance of NCF1-339/NCF1 90H to SLE risk through decreased ROS and interferon signaling, NCF1 90H is a plausible variant to functionally evaluate rather than a conclusion established by the GWAS premise alone."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) A cautious common pattern is that autoimmune disease and SLE risk can involve genetic susceptibility together with environmental factors, including candidate infections, but specific viral causes require direct testing."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) SLE genetics and mouse challenge models together support a general strategy of using defined animal models to investigate how genetic susceptibility and environmental challenges contribute to lupus mechanisms."];
  "R2" [label="(0,0,0) The failure of the Ncf1 90H allele to enhance pristane-induced lupus under specific pathogen-free conditions, together with unresolved evidence about infectious triggers of lupus, supports treating environmental or infectious exposures as hypotheses to test rather than concluding that murine norovirus is already the specific synergistic factor."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) Evidence from Ncf1-mutant mice indicates that lupus-related phenotypes and NCF1-regulated interferon responses can depend on environmental challenge, including pristane or immunization, rather than being fully explained by genotype alone."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) Animal studies in rats and mice identified Ncf1 variants or mutations, in a gene encoding the ROS-related NOX2 component NCF1/p47phox, as relevant to autoimmune disease phenotypes."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Because SLE is genetically complex and specific viral or environmental causes remain unresolved, the evidence motivates studies that evaluate defined genetic susceptibility together with candidate environmental or infectious exposures."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Pristane-induced lupus is a useful mouse model for probing pathogenic mechanisms, and the observation that NCF1-regulated interferon differences are apparent after pristane injection makes pristane a relevant environmental challenge to evaluate in Ncf1-related lupus studies."];
  "abd_phen_mnv" [label="(25,0,0) Observed phenomenon: To our surprise, the Ncf1 90H allele does not enhance pristane-induced lupus in the mice under specific pathogen-free conditions."];
  "ded_case_animal_origin" [label="(8,0,0) Currently there is an amino acid replacing SNP (Ncf1 T153M) associated with autoimmune diseases positioned in rats and reproduced in mice with spontaneous Ncf1 m1J mutation; in humans the locus was difficult due to CNV but a functionally important SNP (R90H) was identified after exon sequencing."];
  "ded_case_gwas" [label="(3,0,0) Currently there is thanks to GWAS hundreds of lupus disease-associated loci identified strengthening the view that SLE is polygenic regulated by variants in immune tolerance/responsiveness loci."];
  "ded_case_pristane" [label="(0,0,0) Currently there is the NCF1-regulated differences in interferon responses obvious after pristane injection triggering more severe lupus."];
  "ded_concl_gwas" [label="(4,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Given the rule that if it has been difficult to precisely pinpoint and functionally confirm the causative factors of SLE, then an alternative approach to identify the underlying genes is needed, and the case that thanks to GWAS hundreds of lupus disease-associated loci have been identified strengthening the view that SLE is polygenic regulated by variants in immune tolerance/responsiveness loci, therefore identification of causative SNPs and inducing environmental factors remains largely unknown and requires alternative approaches (genetic crosses in animals)."];
  "ded_rule_animal_origin" [label="(7,0,0) If the first autoimmune disease-associated gene cloned is Ncf1 (encoding NCF1/p47phox for NOX2 complex responsible for ROS), then positioning causative genes in rats (T153M SNP) and reproducing the effect in mice (m1J mutation) identifies key SNPs for complex autoimmune diseases."];
  "ded_rule_gwas" [label="(2,0,0) If it has been difficult to precisely pinpoint and functionally confirm the causative factors of SLE, then an alternative approach to identify the underlying genes is needed."];
  "ded_rule_ncf1_human" [label="(11,0,0) If analysis of SLE cohorts shows high odds ratio and allelic frequency for NCF1-339 (NCF1 90H), then the variant is a risk factor for SLE via decreased ROS and activated interferon signaling."];
  "ded_rule_pristane" [label="(22,0,0) If pristane-induced lupus is a commonly used mouse model of SLE (as shown in Ncf1 m1J mice), then like several other mouse lupus models it has been extensively studied for pathogenic mechanisms with different downstream causative mechanisms suggested."];
  "ded_rule_trigger" [label="(21,0,0) If NCF1-regulated differences in interferon signaling responses are seen in germ-free mice only after immunization and are obvious after pristane injection (which triggers a more severe lupus-associated response), then the development of lupus in low-ROS NCF1 variants requires an environmental trigger."];
  "ind_case_virus" [label="(17,0,0) Specific case: In humans there is no consensus on specific causative virus infections although DNA viruses (EBV, BKV, RV) have been suggested; no substantial evidence for SARS-CoV-2 triggering lupus but scattered cases reported; Covid-19 triggers presentation/exacerbation of autoimmune diseases in genetically predisposed patients."];
  "ded_rule_gwas" -> "ded_concl_gwas" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "ded_case_gwas" -> "ded_concl_gwas" [label="deduction-case"];
  "abd_phen_mnv" -> "R2" [label="abduction-phenomenon"];
  "ind_case_virus" -> "R2" [label="abduction-knowledge"];
